---
description: Coding conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

# TypeScript

- Use strict TypeScript.
- Never use `any`.
- Prefer explicit types.
- Create shared interfaces when reused.

# React

- Functional components only.
- Keep components focused.
- Avoid components larger than ~200 lines.
- Extract reusable UI.

# Functions

- Prefer small functions.
- One responsibility per function.
- Use early returns.

# Async

Always use:

- async/await

Avoid nested Promise chains.

# Naming

Components

PascalCase

Variables

camelCase

Constants

UPPER_CASE

Files

kebab-case unless framework requires otherwise.

# Imports

Prefer absolute imports where possible.

Group imports:

1. external
2. internal
3. relative

# Comments

Write comments explaining WHY.

Avoid comments explaining WHAT.

# Code Quality

Avoid:

- duplicated logic
- magic numbers
- deeply nested if statements
- giant switch statements

Extract reusable code.